      "Language": "eng",
      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": "In the Salmeterol Multicenter Asthma Research Trial (SMART), patients receiving the long-acting beta agonist salmeterol--particularly African Americans--had a statistically significantly higher risk of fatal or potentially fatal asthma episodes. As a result, medications that contain salmeterol (Serevent, Advair) or formoterol (Foradil) carry a \"black box warning.\" However, the benefits of these drugs continue to outweigh the risks, if they are used appropriately."},
